  libdata[libdataItem++] = new Array("./red__demodulate.html#red::demodulate", "red::demodulate", 'routine in <a href="./red__demodulate.html">red__demodulate.pro</a>', "red__demodulate.pro", "    Mats Löfdahl, Institute for Solar Physics   ", "red::demodulate", " Demodulate restored images for a particular scan and tuning state.   This method does (or at least is meant to do) the same as  pol__demodulate.pro in the master (old CRISP) branch, except that it  reads the inverse modulation matrices from disk rather than having  pointers to them from within the pol class object. (We don't use a  pol class in the new code base.) We rely on red_mozaik to handle  both the inverse mod matrices and the image data the same way when  it comes to clipping.   ", "clips       Used to compute stretch vectors for the wideband alignment.   cmap       The cavity map, to be distorted like the image data and stored        in the stokes cube.   nbrfac       A scaling factor to apply to NBR data to get the correct units.   nbrstates       An array of structs with the states of the input NBR images.   nbtfac       A scaling factor to apply to NBT data to get the correct units.   nbtstates       An array of structs with the states of the input NBT images.   nearestnoremove_periodic       Do not attempt to use Fourier filtering to remove polcal        periodic artifacts.   notelmatnthreads       The number of threads to use.   overwritesmooth_by_kernelsmooth_by_subfieldtiles       Used to compute stretch vectors for the wideband alignment.   unitswbg      The global WB image to use as destretching reference. If this       keyword is not used, no destretching will be done.   wbstates       An array of structs with the states of the input WB images. If        provided, will use them to stretch the NB images when        combining them.   wcsoutname        The file name in which to write the demodulated Stokes cube.   immr        The inverse demodulation matrix for the Crisp-R camera.   immt        The inverse demodulation matrix for the Crisp-T camera.   ", "SST pipeline", "   2018-10-09 : MGL. First version, based on Jaime's pol::demodulate.     2018-12-05 : MGL. New keyword cmap.     2018-12-21 : MGL. New keywords smooth_by_kernel and                 smooth_by_subfield.     2019-12-06 : MGL. New keyword noremove_periodic. Do optional                 Fourier filtering to remove periodic artifacts from                 polcal. Read header info from filter file and include                 filtering in prstep.     2019-04-09 : OA. Added check for NaN values in momfbd files they                 are filled with zeroes (it happens out of the limb).     2020-06-16 : MGL. In FITS header, write SOLARNET recommended                 PRSTEP and POLCCONV.     2020-10-01 : JdlCR. Use the new red_stretch_linear to apply the                 wbcorrection. Also allow for nearest neighbor                 interpolation.     2020-12-09 : MGL. Remove statistics calculations.     2021-10-20 : MGL. Save some time by storing smoothed versions of                 the inverse demodulation matrices.     2021-12-10 : JdlCR. Make use of the new libgrid routines, now                 ported to rdx and maintainable by us.     2022-07-29 : MGL. Change from a CRISP:: method to a RED:: method.     2025-01-22 : MGL. Set step PRMODE for new demodulation /                 flat-fielding scheme.     2025-02-04 : MGL. Added the telescope calibration model parameters                 and the telescope Mueller matrix as PRREF to the                 demodulation step information.     2025-02-20 : MGL. Adapt to new camera alignment model.     2025-05-28 : MGL. Adapt to mix of polarimetric and                 non-polarimetric data. New keyword notelmat.    ");
  
  

libdata[libdataItem++] = new Array("./red__diversitycalib.html", "red__diversitycalib.pro", '.pro file in <a href="./dir-overview.html">./ directory</a>', "red__diversitycalib.pro", "", "", "", "", "          -1", "");
  
  
  libdata[libdataItem++] = new Array("./red__diversitycalib.html#red::diversitycalib", "red::diversitycalib", 'routine in <a href="./red__diversitycalib.html">red__diversitycalib.pro</a>', "red__diversitycalib.pro", "    Mats Löfdahl, ISP, 2017   ", "red::diversitycalib", "   Find the amount of defocusing of the diversity camera.   ", "threshold       Threshold for identifying a strong enough pinhole.   nref      How many of the strongest pinholes to use for finding the       approximate transform. Afterwards a refinement is made using       &gt;80% of the detected pinholes.   pref      Indicate the prefilter you want to calculate the clips for,       Default is to do it for all prefilters there is data for.   dirnslavesnthreadsverbose", "SST pipeline", "      2017-01-25 : MGL. First version.   ");
  
  

libdata[libdataItem++] = new Array("./red__download.html", "red__download.pro", '.pro file in <a href="./dir-overview.html">./ directory</a>', "red__download.pro", "", "", "", "", "          -1", "");
  
  
  libdata[libdataItem++] = new Array("./red__download.html#red::download", "red::download", 'routine in <a href="./red__download.html">red__download.pro</a>', "red__download.pro", "    Mats Löfdahl, 2013-12-16   ", "red::download", " Downloads logfiles and other useful auxiliary data when and if  needed. Puts them in subdirectory downloads/.   ", "overwrite      Set this to download without checking if the file already exists.   all      Try to download all types of data.   logs      Try to download SST log files. This is the default operation in       case no particular target is specified and all is also not       specified.   pig      Try to download the SST/PIG log file. Returns with the       downloaded file name (or empty string in case download failed).   pathpig      The path to where the pig log file was saved (or the empty       string).   linedefsr0      Try to download the SST/AO r0 log file. Returns with the       downloaded file name (or empty string in case download failed).   pathr0      The path to where the r0 log file was saved (or the empty       string).   pathturret      The path to where the turret log file was saved (or the empty       string).   turret      Try to download the SST/Turret log file. Returns with the       downloaded file name (or empty string in case download failed).   armap      Try to download the Active Regions map.   hmi      Try to download HMI images and movies.   backscatter      Set this to [ 8542 ,  7772 ] (or a subset thereof) to download       backscatter gain and psf for the corresponding prefilter(s).   ", "SST observations", "    2013-12-19 : MGL. Let red_geturl do more of the testing. And also                  make softlinks to the log files. Make the overwrite                  keyword work.      2013-12-20 : MGL. Optionally return file names in r0file,                  turretfile, and pigfile keywords. Do not make soft                  links.      2014-01-04 : MGL. For turret, now downloads the file for the                  specified date as well as the first existing file                  earlier in time. Do this without writing to disk.                  Concatenate the downloaded turret data, select only                  the relevant lines, and save to the turret file to                  be used by the pipeline.      2014-01-08 : MGL. Make downloading logs the default.      2014-01-08 : MGL. Turn it into a method in order to access                  members, like the date and directory names. Remove                  the date keyword.      2014-01-10 : MGL. Do not try to remove files if the file name is                  the empty string.      2014-01-22 : MGL. Adapt to string functions moved to the str_                  namespace.      2015-09-25 : MGL. Don't download the PIG logfile unless                  asked for.      2016-02-15 : MGL. Added downloading of backscatter data files for                  8542 and 7772 prefilters.      2016-02-17 : MGL. Use file name provided by red::loadbackscatter                  rather than constructiong one.      2016-02-19 : MGL. Transform backscatter psf the same way as the                  backscatter gain.      2016-02-24 : MGL. Make backscatter renaming work also for years                  prior to 2012.      2017-04-12 : MGL. Pig log can have isodate or dotdate in the                  path. Use new convertlog as DLM and not separate                  executable.      2017-08-18 : THI. Also download the FPI calibration values                  (linedef.py). Include FPI calibration in implied                  downloads.      2021-08-27 : MGL. Use red_download_log for r0 and PIG log files.                  Include the PIG log files in the logs category.   ");
  
  

libdata[libdataItem++] = new Array("./red__extractstates.html", "red__extractstates.pro", '.pro file in <a href="./dir-overview.html">./ directory</a>', "red__extractstates.pro", "", "", "", "", "          -1", "");
  
  
  libdata[libdataItem++] = new Array("./red__extractstates.html#red::extractstates", "red::extractstates", 'routine in <a href="./red__extractstates.html">red__extractstates.pro</a>', "red__extractstates.pro", "     Oleksii Andriienko, ISP   ", "red::extractstates", " Extract states information from an array of strings (typically file  names).   Substitutes original crisp__extractstates.pro and  chromis__extractstates.pro that were copied to  crisp__extractstates_nondb.pro and chromis__extractstates_nondb.pro,  respectively. This procedure is a wrapper around db and nondb  versions.   ", "camdatasets        List of datasets timestamps to be used instead of list of         filenames. Can be used only if sst_db is installed.   force        Do not use cached states.   nondb polcal        Set this to add polcal-specific items in the states, qw and         lp.   strip_settings        Exclude exposure/gain information from the fullstate entries.   strings        A list of strings from which to extract the states         information.   states        An array of structs, containing (partially filled) state         information.   ", "SSTRED", "   2019-07-23 : OA. Created.     2022-07-29 : MGL. Change from a CRISP:: method to a RED:: method                 to prepare for CRISP camera upgrade.    ");
  
  

libdata[libdataItem++] = new Array("./red__fit_nb_diskcenter.html", "red__fit_nb_diskcenter.pro", '.pro file in <a href="./dir-overview.html">./ directory</a>', "red__fit_nb_diskcenter.pro", "", "", "", "", "          -1", "");
  
  
  libdata[libdataItem++] = new Array("./red__fit_nb_diskcenter.html#red::fit_nb_diskcenter", "red::fit_nb_diskcenter", 'routine in <a href="./red__fit_nb_diskcenter.html">red__fit_nb_diskcenter.pro</a>', "red__fit_nb_diskcenter.pro", "    Mats Löfdahl, ISP   ", "red::fit_nb_diskcenter", " Measure median disk center narrowband intensities and fit to function  of time.   Based on red::fit_wb_diskcenter.pro   ", "demodulatedirs        Set this to the time-stamp directories to use to limit the         automatic selection. Useful for excluding, e.g., data with a         large sunspot in the field of view.   exclude_dirs        Set this to the time-stamp directories to exclude from         the automatically selected directories, or from the         directories specified with the dirs keyword.   fitexpr        The expression that is fit to the intensities by use of         mpfitexpr. An integer is interpreted as shorthand for a         polynomial of that degree.   limb_darkening        Correct intensities for distance from disk center.   mu_limit        WB data collected farther from disk center than this are         excluded automatically. The default depends on whether         correction for limb_darkening is in effect.   pref        Process data only for this prefilter.   tmin        Do not use datasets started before this time, specified using         the format  HH[[:MM]:SS] .   tmax        Do not use datasets started after this time, specified using         the format  HH[[:MM]:SS] . Useful if, e.g., there are both AM         and PM data, and the fit is not good if both are included.   ", "SST pipeline", "    2021-09-09 : MGL. First version.      2021-10-19 : MGL. New keyword /demodulate.   ");
  
  

libdata[libdataItem++] = new Array("./red__fit_wb_diskcenter.html", "red__fit_wb_diskcenter.pro", '.pro file in <a href="./dir-overview.html">./ directory</a>', "red__fit_wb_diskcenter.pro", "", "", "", "", "          -1", "");
  
  
  libdata[libdataItem++] = new Array("./red__fit_wb_diskcenter.html#red::fit_wb_diskcenter", "red::fit_wb_diskcenter", 'routine in <a href="./red__fit_wb_diskcenter.html">red__fit_wb_diskcenter.pro</a>', "red__fit_wb_diskcenter.pro", "    Mats Löfdahl, ISP   ", "red::fit_wb_diskcenter", " Measure median disk center wideband intensities and fit to function  of time.   The use of the median means it is OK to include data with pores or  even a small spot in the FOV.   ", "dirs        Set this to the time-stamp directories to use to limit the         automatic selection. Useful for excluding, e.g., data with a         large sunspot in the field of view.   exclude_dirs        Set this to the time-stamp directories to exclude from         the automatically selected directories, or from the         directories specified with the dirs keyword.   fitexpr        The expression that is fit to the intensities by use of         mpfitexpr. An integer is interpreted as shorthand for a         polynomial of that degree.   limb_darkening        Correct intensities for distance from disk center.   mu_limit        WB data collected farther from disk center than this are         excluded automatically. The default depends on whether         correction for limb_darkening is in effect.   pref        Process data only for this prefilter.   sum_all_framestmin        Do not use datasets started before this time, specified using         the format  HH[[:MM]:SS] .   tmax        Do not use datasets started after this time, specified using         the format  HH[[:MM]:SS] . Useful if, e.g., there are both AM         and PM data, and the fit is not good if both are included.   overwrite", "SST pipeline", "    2019-07-15 : MGL. First version.      2020-01-15 : MGL. New keywords tmin and tmax. If mu unavailable                  in logs, assume flats are at large enough mu.      2020-01-20 : MGL. Use data from every 20th scan.      2021-08-27 : MGL. New keyword exclude_dirs.      2021-09-06 : MGL. New keyword limb_darkening.   ");
  
  

libdata[libdataItem++] = new Array("./red__fitgains.html", "red__fitgains.pro", '.pro file in <a href="./dir-overview.html">./ directory</a>', "red__fitgains.pro", "", "", "", "", "          -1", "");
  
  
  libdata[libdataItem++] = new Array("./red__fitgains.html#red::fitgains", "red::fitgains", 'routine in <a href="./red__fitgains.html">red__fitgains.pro</a>', "red__fitgains.pro", " ", "red::fitgains", " ", "all       If set, bypass selection and process all data.   densegrid extra_nodes       Make extra spline nodes at the specified wavelengths, given in        Ångström from the core point.   fit_reflectivity       Fit reflectivity in addition to cavity map.   initcmap       Initialize the cavity map.   myg       Specify the wavelength nodes, alternative to using the data        tuning points.   niter       Number of iterations.   nosave       Do not save the output.   npar       Number of additional terms (default: 1 = linear)   nthreads       Number of threads used by red_cfitgain and red_cfitgain2.   pref       Process data for this prefilter.   rebin res       The results of the fit, including the cavity map.   thres w0      The index of the lowest wavelength point to include in the fit.       Use this if necessary to deselect blue points that are too far       from each other.   w1      The index of the highest wavelength point to include in the       fit. Use this if necessary to deselect red points that are too       far from each other.   x0 x1 xl yl sig ", "CRISP pipeline", "   2013-06-04 : Split from monolithic version of crispred.pro.     2013-08-27 : MGL. Added support for logging. Let the subprogram                 find out its own name.     2013-12-20 : PS join with _ng version: reflectivity as keyword,                 npar is number of *additional* terms (default: 1 =                 linear)     2013-12-21 : MGL. Changed default npar to 2.     2016-03-22 : JLF. Added support for .lc4 flat cubes (see   	 	 red::prepflatcubes_lc4). Added a bit of error checking.     2016-10-04 : MGL. Adapted for CHROMIS data and split_classes. Set                 up for red_get_imean to use cgplot so plots can                 easily be saved. Individual npar defaults for                 prefilters, so we can batch process. Get output file                 names from filenames method.     2016-10-26 : MGL. Special case for prefilters with only a single                 wavelength point.     2017-04-13 : MGL. Make SOLARNET FITS headers.     2017-04-20 : MGL. New keyword extra_nodes.     2018-06-08 : MGL. New keyword pref.     2022-09-01 : MGL. Automatically mask bad pixels and pixels without                 light.     2023-11-02 : JdlCR. Modifications for multiple LC fitting with                 a single cavity map value for the new demodulation                 and flat-fielding scheme.    ");
  
  

libdata[libdataItem++] = new Array("./red__fitprefilter.html", "red__fitprefilter.pro", '.pro file in <a href="./dir-overview.html">./ directory</a>', "red__fitprefilter.pro", "", "", "", "", "          -1", "");
  
  
  libdata[libdataItem++] = new Array("./red__fitprefilter.html#red::fitprefilter", "red::fitprefilter", 'routine in <a href="./red__fitprefilter.html">red__fitprefilter.pro</a>', "red__fitprefilter.pro", " ", "red::fitprefilter", " ", "fixcav w0 w1 pref noasy shift initstretchweightmask", "CRISP pipeline", "   2013-06-04 : Split from monolithic version of crispred.pro.     2013-07-11 : MGL. Use red_satlas rather than satlas. Use                 red_intepf rather than intepf.     2013-08-27 : MGL. Added support for logging. Let the subprogram                 find out its own name.     2015-05-05 : MGL. If keyword pref is given, use it when looking                 for files.     2016-03-22 : JLF. Added support for lc4 flat cubes (see                 modifications to red::prepflatcubes_lc4). Changed                 'pref' keyword to 'state' and made its behavior                 similar to red::fitgains. Added some error checking.     2016-04-01 : THI. Changed 'state' keyword back to 'pref' for now,                 so that old scripts do not need to be modified.     2016-10-13 : MGL. Adapted to CHROMIS and new pipeline mechanisms.     2016-10-27 : MGL. Special case for prefilters with only a single                 wavelength point.     2017-02-14 : JdlCR. Added the option to mask a region of the FOV.    ");
  
  

libdata[libdataItem++] = new Array("./red__fitscube_addvarkeyword.html", "red__fitscube_addvarkeyword.pro", '.pro file in <a href="./dir-overview.html">./ directory</a>', "red__fitscube_addvarkeyword.pro", "", "", "", "", "          -1", "");
  
  
  libdata[libdataItem++] = new Array("./red__fitscube_addvarkeyword.html#red::fitscube_addvarkeyword", "red::fitscube_addvarkeyword", 'routine in <a href="./red__fitscube_addvarkeyword.html">red__fitscube_addvarkeyword.pro</a>', "red__fitscube_addvarkeyword.pro", "    Mats Löfdahl, Institute for Solar Physics   ", "red::fitscube_addvarkeyword", " Add data to a FITS file using the Variable-Keyword mechanism of the  SOLARNET document, appendix I.   To make implementation easier, we'll have each keyword in an  extension of its own. The extenstion's name is  VAR-EXT-  followed  by the name of the keyword.   ", "old_filenameaxis_numbers       For a pixel-to-pixel association with, e.g., NAXIS2 and        NAXIS4, use axis_numbers=[2,4].     flipped : in, optional, type=boolean         Set this if the keyword should be added to a  flipped  cube.        Only needed for coordinate-association keywords but does no        harm for other association types.     comment : in, optional, type=string         The keyword comment in the main header.     keyword_value : in, optional, type=varies         The keyword value in the main header.     keyword_method : in, optional, type=string, default='first'         The keyword value in the main header to be calculated with        this method. One of 'first', 'last', 'mean', 'median', 'min',        'max'.     old_filename : in, optional, type=string         If this is given, any values parameter (and many other        keywords) will be ignored and the information will be        collected from this file instead.     _ref_extra :  in, optional         Any extra keywords are used when positioning keywords in the        main header, see red_fitsaddkeyword.   keyword_valuekeyword_methodcommenttunitextra_coordinate1extra_coordinate2extra_labelsextra_namesextra_unitsspatial_coordinatesspatial_deltasspatial_unitstime_coordinatetime_deltatime_unitwavelength_coordinateswavelength_deltawavelength_unitsflipped_ref_extrafilename       The name of the file in which to add the variable-keyword.   keyword_name       The name of the keyword.   values      The values of the variable-keyword. If this is not given,       keyword old_filename must be given and the keyword will be       taken from there.   ", "SST pipeline", "   2017-09-06 : MGL. First version, supporting pixel-to-pixel                 association and coordinate association for tabulated                 time.     2017-09-07 : MGL. Changed red_fitsaddpar --&gt; red_fitsaddkeyword.     2017-09-08 : MGL. New keyword old_filename.     2017-09-13 : MGL. New keyword flipped.     2018-06-13 : MGL. New keyword keyword_method. Allow keyword                 positioning keywords.   ");
  
  

libdata[libdataItem++] = new Array("./red__fitscube_addwcs.html", "red__fitscube_addwcs.pro", '.pro file in <a href="./dir-overview.html">./ directory</a>', "red__fitscube_addwcs.pro", "", "", "", "", "          -1", "");
  
  
  libdata[libdataItem++] = new Array("./red__fitscube_addwcs.html#red::fitscube_addwcs", "red::fitscube_addwcs", 'routine in <a href="./red__fitscube_addwcs.html">red__fitscube_addwcs.pro</a>', "red__fitscube_addwcs.pro", "    Mats Löfdahl, ISP   ", "red::fitscube_addwcs", " Add a WCS extension to a fitscube file.   This was inspired by Stein's wcs_crosstabulation.pro   ", "dimensions       The dimensions of the data cube.   no_extension       Only add the header keywords, not the extension.   filename       The name of the file.   wcs       The WCS coordinates hpln, hplt, wave, time as fltarr(2, 2,        Ntunes, Nscans) arrays.   ", "SST pipeline", "    2016-03-24 : MGL. First version.      2016-08-25 : MGL. Add spatial coordinates.      2016-09-28 : MGL. Add a new parameter wcs.      2016-10-11 : MGL. Remove keywords                  wcs_{hpln,hplt,wave,time}_coordinate.      2017-10-18 : MGL. WCS related file header keywords moved here                  from fitscube_initialize method. New keyword                  dimensions.      2018-01-16 : MGL. Allow for degenerate trailing dimensions of                  scan-only cubes.      2018-11-29 : MGL. New keyword no_extension.   ");
  
  

libdata[libdataItem++] = new Array("./red__fitscube_cmapcorr.html", "red__fitscube_cmapcorr.pro", '.pro file in <a href="./dir-overview.html">./ directory</a>', "red__fitscube_cmapcorr.pro", "", "", "", "", "          -1", "");
  
  
  libdata[libdataItem++] = new Array("./red__fitscube_cmapcorr.html#red::fitscube_cmapcorr", "red::fitscube_cmapcorr", 'routine in <a href="./red__fitscube_cmapcorr.html">red__fitscube_cmapcorr.pro</a>', "red__fitscube_cmapcorr.pro", "    Mats Löfdahl, Institute for Solar Physics   ", "red::fitscube_cmapcorr", " Make a fitscube that is corrected for wavelength distortions (cavity  errors).   ", "flip       Produce a flipped version if this keywoed is set.   interpolmethod       The interpolation method to use.   outname       The name of the output file.   overwrite       Don't care if the output cube is already on disk, overwrite it        with a new version.   _extra      Any extra keywords are used when calling the chosen       interpolation method.   fname       The name of the input file.   ", "SST pipeline", "   2018-11-02 : MGL. First version.     2018-12-06 : MGL. Additional interpolation methods.     2019-09-27 : MGL. Implement correction of individual cavity maps                 for multiple prefilters.   ");
  
  

libdata[libdataItem++] = new Array("./red__fitscube_concatenate.html", "red__fitscube_concatenate.pro", '.pro file in <a href="./dir-overview.html">./ directory</a>', "red__fitscube_concatenate.pro", "", "", "", "", "          -1", "");
  
  
  libdata[libdataItem++] = new Array("./red__fitscube_concatenate.html#red::fitscube_concatenate", "red::fitscube_concatenate", 'routine in <a href="./red__fitscube_concatenate.html">red__fitscube_concatenate.pro</a>', "red__fitscube_concatenate.pro", "    Mats Löfdahl, Institute for Solar Physics   ", "red::fitscube_concatenate", " Concatenate multiple fitscubes (nb or scan) into a single fitscube.   Based on assumption that the input fitscubes have the same tuning  points and polarimetry status. They should also share the same  (approximate) pointing. They are separated in time and are all  derotated to Solar N up. It is the user's responsibility to  make sure this is the case.   Do not use already concatenated files or multi-dataset nb cubes as  input!   ", "noflipping      Do not make a spectral cube version.   overwrite      Overwrite existing outfile.   point_id      Value for the POINT_ID header keyword. By default the value if       POINT_ID in the temporally first file or, if that does not       exist, the value of DATE-OBS in the temporally first file.   infiles      Array of file names/paths of fitscube files to concatenate into       a single file.   outfile      File name/path for the concatenated fitscube.   ", "SST pipeline", "   2021-11-18 : MGL. First version.    ");
  
  

libdata[libdataItem++] = new Array("./red__fitscube_convertlp.html", "red__fitscube_convertlp.pro", '.pro file in <a href="./dir-overview.html">./ directory</a>', "red__fitscube_convertlp.pro", "", "", "", "", "          -1", "");
  
  
  libdata[libdataItem++] = new Array("./red__fitscube_convertlp.html#red::fitscube_convertlp", "red::fitscube_convertlp", 'routine in <a href="./red__fitscube_convertlp.html">red__fitscube_convertlp.pro</a>', "red__fitscube_convertlp.pro", "    Mats Löfdahl, Institute for Solar Physics   ", "red::fitscube_convertlp", " Convert an old LP format science data cube to a fitscube.   ", "cavitymaps      A 3D cube with cavity maps, each adapted to the corresponding       scan in the fitscube file. Unit is nm.   direction      The relative orientation of reference cameras of different       instruments. Note that only if direction is set in the config       file will it be assumed to be correct when setting the CSYERR       FITS header keyword.   dorotate      We will assume multi-scan cubes are de-rotated to compensate       for the alt-az field rotation and also rotated to Solar-N up.       Set this keyword to assume only the former and therefore make       the rotation to the proper orientation.   flipheaderfile      The name of a file where headerdata can be found.   mirrorx      The cube wb data are mirrored in the X direction compared to       the raw data.   mirrory      The cube wb data are mirrored in the Y direction compared to       the raw data.   outdiroutname      Where to write the output. A spectral cube might also be       written, the file name for this will be generated based on       outname. If a variable, will be returned with the actual file       name.   overwrite       Don't care if cube is already on disk, overwrite it        with a new version.   point_id      Value for the POINT_ID header keyword.   prefrotation      Offset angle to be added to the field rotation angles.   scannumbers      The scan numbers of the scans in the cube as a dash- and       comma-delimited string.   timestampwbimagefile      Path to a file with a wideband image to be added as a contect       image for a single-scan file.   inname       The path to the file to be converted.   ", "SST pipeline", "    2017-12-06 : MGL. First version.      2018-05-30 : MGL. Works also with CRISP data.      2021-11-26 : MGL. New default output dir and use                  red_fitscube_filename() for the filename. New                  keywords point_id, wbimagefile, direction, rotation.                  Remove keyword nostatistics (and statistics                  calculations). Various minor bug fixes.   ");
  
  

libdata[libdataItem++] = new Array("./red__fitscube_crop.html", "red__fitscube_crop.pro", '.pro file in <a href="./dir-overview.html">./ directory</a>', "red__fitscube_crop.pro", "", "", "", "", "          -1", "");
  
  
  libdata[libdataItem++] = new Array("./red__fitscube_crop.html#red::fitscube_crop", "red::fitscube_crop", 'routine in <a href="./red__fitscube_crop.html">red__fitscube_crop.pro</a>', "red__fitscube_crop.pro", "    Mats Löfdahl, Institute for Solar Physics   ", "red::fitscube_crop", " Crop a fitscube while maintaining meta data.   ", "centered      Set this to get a centered FOV. Specify the size with the size       keyword or   iscan      Select image to display in xroi GUI by setting ituning, istokes,       and/or iscan. Indices not specified signals a dimension to sum       over.   istokes      Select image to display in xroi GUI by setting ituning,       istokes, and/or iscan. Indices not specified signals a       dimension to sum over.   ituning      Select image to display in xroi GUI by setting ituning, istokes,       and/or iscan. Indices not specified signals a dimension to sum       over.   nospectral      If set, don't make any spectral,  flipped  data cubes.   outfile      The name of the file in which to store the cropped cube.   overwrite      Set this to overwrite older files.   roi      Give the ROI corner coordinates [llx,urx,lly,ury] to bypass       interactive FOV selection. If the FOV is selected interactively       and/or specified with the size and centered keywords the roi is       returned in this keyword.   size      Set this to a FOV size to only select center of FOV       interactively. If an array, it is interpreted as sx=size[0],       sy=size[1]. If a single integer, sx=sy=size.   xc      X pixel coordinate of center of FOV.   yc      Y pixel coordinate of center of FOV.   infile      The name of the file containing the fitscube to be cropped.   ", "SST pipeline", "    2017-11-08 : MGL. First version.      2017-11-10 : MGL. Copy (and modify when needed) extensions.                  Renamed keyword corners to roi and changed the order                  of elements.      2018-01-12 : MGL. Use subroutine red_fitscube_getframe rather                  than method fitscube_getframe.   ");
  
  

libdata[libdataItem++] = new Array("./red__fitscube_crosstalk.html", "red__fitscube_crosstalk.pro", '.pro file in <a href="./dir-overview.html">./ directory</a>', "red__fitscube_crosstalk.pro", "", "", "", "", "          -1", "");
  
  
  libdata[libdataItem++] = new Array("./red__fitscube_crosstalk.html#fitscube_crosstalk_event", "fitscube_crosstalk_event", 'routine in <a href="./red__fitscube_crosstalk.html">red__fitscube_crosstalk.pro</a>', "red__fitscube_crosstalk.pro", "", "fitscube_crosstalk_event", "", "event", "          -1", "");
  
  libdata[libdataItem++] = new Array("./red__fitscube_crosstalk.html#red::fitscube_crosstalk", "red::fitscube_crosstalk", 'routine in <a href="./red__fitscube_crosstalk.html">red__fitscube_crosstalk.pro</a>', "red__fitscube_crosstalk.pro", "    Mats Löfdahl, Institute for Solar Physics   ", "red::fitscube_crosstalk", " Correct a polarimetric fitscube for crosstalk from I to Q, U, and V.   ", "flip       Produce a flipped version if this keyword is set.   force       Do not care if the correction is done already.   mag_mask       A mask that deselects magnetic signal. Should have the same        dimensions as a frame. Use keyword primarily to preserve a        mask from one call to the next so user only has to to use the        GUI once.   margin       Remove this many pixels from all edges when making the        magnetic mask.   testtuning_selection       The index or indices in the tuning dimension to use for        calculating the correction. Should correspond to continuum (or        as close to continuum as possible), where the polarimetric        signal is minimal. Negative indices are allowed. Keyword can        be used to preserve a mask from one call to the next so user        only has to to use the GUI once.   filename       The name of the file containing the polarimetric fitscube.   ", "SST pipeline", "   2019-04-01 : MGL. First version.     2019-04-04 : MGL. New keywords nostatistics and tuning_selection.     2019-04-05 : MGL. Use red_fitscube_open and red_fitscube_close.     2020-03-23 : OA. Changed calls of red_fitscube_getframe &                 *_addframe with fileassoc instead of filename. Added                 keyword 'fitscube_info' in those calls.     2020-10-28 : MGL. Remove statistics calculations.     2021-04-15 : MGL. Improved magnetic mask construction. New keyword                 margin.     2021-05-05 : MGL. New GUI for constructing the magnetic mask.   ");
  
  

libdata[libdataItem++] = new Array("./red__fitscube_export.html", "red__fitscube_export.pro", '.pro file in <a href="./dir-overview.html">./ directory</a>', "red__fitscube_export.pro", "", "", "", "", "          -1", "");
  
  
  libdata[libdataItem++] = new Array("./red__fitscube_export.html#red::fitscube_export", "red::fitscube_export", 'routine in <a href="./red__fitscube_export.html">red__fitscube_export.pro</a>', "red__fitscube_export.pro", "    Mats Löfdahl, Institute for Solar Physics   ", "red::fitscube_export", " Make an adjusted version of a fitscube that is suitable for  exporting to an SVO, and copy it to its archival directory.   Copy also the spectral cube, if there is one.   ", "helpkeywords      Keywords and values to be added to the header. Keywords are       upcased and checked against a list of SOLARNET-approved       keywords.   no_spectral_file      Do not copy the sp version of the input file, if there is one.   no_wb_fileno_thumbnail      Do not make a thumbnail image.   no_video      Do not make a video.   outdir      The directory in which to store the new file/to which the file       was exported.   outfile      The name of the file to which the data were exported.   overwrite      Set this to overwrite an existing file.   smooth_width      If present, blur all images in the exported cube with       smooth(frame, blur). This is to facilitate making sample cubes       without actually releasing data. If unity, interpreted as a       boolean and set to a default width of 11 pixels.   svo_api_key      Ingest the metadata of the cube into the prototype SVO using       this API_KEY.   svo_username      Ingest the metadata of the cube into the prototype SVO using       this USERNAME.   thumb_shrink_fac      If making a thumbnail image, shrink it by this factor.   video_shrink_fac      If making a video, shrink the FOV by this factor.   allowed_usersswedish_datatrust_datasum      Set this keyword to avoid checking datasum.   filename      The path of the fitscube file.   ", "SST pipeline", "   2019-06-12 : MGL. First version.     2019-06-17 : MGL. New keyword help.     2019-06-18 : MGL. New keywords smooth_width and outfile. Add                 prstep header info.     2019-07-04 : MGL. Optionally (opt-out) add checksum and datasum.     2019-10-18 : MGL. New keywords svo_api_key and svo_username.     2020-11-02 : MGL. Remove stuff that is now in fitscube_finalize.     2020-12-04 : MGL. Generate an OID.     2020-12-07 : MGL. Generate thumbnail image and video.     2020-12-10 : MGL. New keywords thumb_shrink_fac and                 video_shrink_fac.     2021-01-11 : OA. Submit information about exported cubes to the                 database.     2022-03-24 : OA. Added trust_datasum keyword.   ");
  
  

