  libdata[libdataItem++] = new Array("./red_crop.html#red_crop", "red_crop", 'routine in <a href="./red_crop.html">red_crop.pro</a>', "red_crop.pro", "    Mats Löfdahl, Institute for Solar Physics   ", "red_crop", " Crop an image or image cube, out-of-bounds pixels.   A 3D array is interpreted as an image cube where the first two  dimensions are spatial.   If no or only partial FOV information is given with keywords, use  the XROI GUI to either modify an initial ROI/FOV or define a new one  from scratch. The last ROI is used.   ", "centered      Set this to get a centered FOV.   roi      ROI corner coordinates [llx,urx,lly,ury]. If the roi is       selected specified with other keywords the roi is returned in       this keyword.   nocropping      Don't actually do any cropping, return after establishing       the  roi  keyword.   pad      Either a number used to fill in out-of-bounds pixels or a       string with a method to calculate such a number from the       cropped image ( mean  or  median ).   size      Set this to a FOV size to only select center of FOV       interactively. If an array, it is interpreted as sx=size[0],       sy=size[1]. If a single integer, sx=sy=size.   xc      X pixel coordinate of center of FOV.   yc      Y pixel coordinate of center of FOV.   ims      An image or an image cube (up to 8 dimensions, where the first       two are the image dimensions) to be cropped.   ", "SST pipeline", "    2017-11-06 : MGL. First version.      2017-11-07 : MGL. New keyword nocropping. Use the XROI GUI to                  define the corners if keywords do not provide enough                  information.      2017-11-09 : MGL. Renamed keyword corners to roi and changed the                  order of elements.       A cropped and possibly padded version of the input array.   ");
  
  

