libdata[libdataItem++] = new Array("./red_currentsite.html", "red_currentsite.pro", '.pro file in <a href="./dir-overview.html">./ directory</a>', "red_currentsite.pro", "", "", "", "", "          -1", "");
  
  
  libdata[libdataItem++] = new Array("./red_currentsite.html#red_currentsite", "red_currentsite", 'routine in <a href="./red_currentsite.html">red_currentsite.pro</a>', "red_currentsite.pro", "    Mats Löfdahl, Institute for Solar Physics   ", "red_currentsite", " Figure out the current site and default data directories and  similar.   Old 'hostname -I' doesn't work on La Palma under an old OpenSuSE installation  therefore the only supported keyword there is -i that gives the right  IP-address on La Palma but not in Stockholm.  There are more robust but less  trivial ways to get the IPv4-address of the machine.  As for 31 July 2017, the  following works:    $ ip addr show | grep -Po 'inet \K[\d.]+'  or    $ /sbin/ifconfig -a | grep -Po 't addr:\K[\d.]+'  Both produce a list of IPv4-addresses for each network interface on La Palma  as well as in Stockholm.  You can narrow the list to only one address by  specifying 'ip addr show eth0' or '/sbin/ifconfig eth0' but it is better to  use full listing as some interfaces might be temporarily off the network.   ", "date      The date in ISO format, needed to construct the search_dir for       some sites.   dnsdomainname      The output of shell command dnsdomainname.   ipv4addresses      The found ipv4 addresses.   search_dirs      Where to search for raw data. Could be an array or a single       string.   site      A string identifying the current site, like  AlbaNova ,  La       Palma , etc.   ", "SST pipeline", "    2017-08-15 : MGL. First version based on logic by Andrii                  Sukhorukov.      2017-08-29 : MGL. Use dnsdomainname to match also nodes that do                  not have world-wide ipv4 addresses. New keywords                  ipv4addresses and dnsdomainname.      2017-08-30 : AVS. Call message instead of inam. Some code                  clean-up.      2018-02-07 : MGL. New search directory structure for AlbaNova.   ");
  
  

