  libdata[libdataItem++] = new Array("./red_find_instrumentdirs.html#red_find_instrumentdirs", "red_find_instrumentdirs", 'routine in <a href="./red_find_instrumentdirs.html">red_find_instrumentdirs.pro</a>', "red_find_instrumentdirs.pro", "    Mats Löfdahl, ISP, 2016-05-05   ", "red_find_instrumentdirs", " Look recursively for instrument-specific subdirectory below a given  directory.   Subdirectories will be searched for by using regular expressions of  the following type:   topdir+'/'+data_prefix+'*/'+levels+instrument_prefix+'*' , where  levels consist of an increasing number of repetitions of  */ . Once  matching subdirectories are found at a certain level, the search  will not go deeper.   ", "sublevels       The max number of levels of subdirectories to search.   count       The number of found subdirectories.   fold       Whether to fold cases when searching.   topdir       Look for directories below this one.   instrument_prefix       A string matching the instrument specific directories, like         crisp  or  chromis .   data_prefix       A string matching the data type directory, like  dark  or         flat .   ", "SST observations", "    2016-05-05 : MGL. Inital version.       A string array with directory names.   ");
  
  

