  libdata[libdataItem++] = new Array("./red_fitscube_filename.html#red_fitscube_filename", "red_fitscube_filename", 'routine in <a href="./red_fitscube_filename.html">red_fitscube_filename.pro</a>', "red_fitscube_filename.pro", "    Mats Löfdahl, Institute for Solar Physics   ", "red_fitscube_filename", " Construct a file name for a fitscube.   ", "datatags      Tags to be added to the filename. Might be used to tell       different versions apart.   oldname      For data from a single datestamp directory, construct the       filename as before multiple directories were implemented.   filetype       One of  wb  and  nb .   prefilter       The four-digit string identifying the prefilter.   timestamps       The timestamp directories contributing data to the fitscube.   scannos       The scannumbers for each timestamp directory represented as a        comma- and dash-delimited string. Should have the same number        of elements as the timestamps parameter.   point_id       A string identifying the observation. Typically the DATE-OBS        or STARTOBS keyword of data from the first timestamp directory        with the same pointing.   ", "SST pipeline", "   2021-11-28 : MGL. First version.       A fitscube filename constructed by use of the input data.   ");
  
  

