libdata[libdataItem++] = new Array("./red_readdata.html", "red_readdata.pro", '.pro file in <a href="./dir-overview.html">./ directory</a>', "red_readdata.pro", "", "", "", "", "          -1", "");
  
  
  libdata[libdataItem++] = new Array("./red_readdata.html#red_readdata", "red_readdata", 'routine in <a href="./red_readdata.html">red_readdata.pro</a>', "red_readdata.pro", "     Mats Löfdahl, ISP, 2016-05-16   ", "red_readdata", " Camera-independent read routine.   ", "dark       The dark frame associated with the momfbd file to be read.        Needed if the keyword rawstatistics is used.   extension	Read from a FITS extension with extname taken from the value of 	extension keyword. If it is an image extension the image is returned. 	If it is a binary or ASCII table the column data are returned which  	correspond to the value of tabkey (or by default the 1st column).  	The extension header is returned in the header keyword (if specified)   date_beg       DATE-BEG keywords for all frames.   direction       Apply red_rotate(...,direction) to the data.   filetype	The type of file to read. Allowed values are: 		fits 		ana                momfbd 	If not set auto-detection will be attempted.   header  	Output the header.   nslice       Read just this frame from a data cube. (Implemented only for        FITS files for now, and that needs some work, too.)   patch_indx       WHen reading a momfbd file, return only this single patch. Set        on output if patch_coord is used.   patch_coord       WHen reading a momfbd file, return only the patch with these        coordinates as specified with the SIM_X/Y/XY momfbd        configuration keywords. Set on output if patch_indx is used.   rawstatistics       Calculate statistics for the raw data that went into the        restored image in the momfbd file to be read.   silentstatus	Output the return status, 0 for success, -1 for failure.   structheader	If set output the header as a structure.   tabkey	The name of the tabulated keyword to extract from the table.   fname       The file name.   ", "CRISP pipeline", "   2016-05-16 : MGL. First version     2016-05-17 : MGL. Default for filetype based on file name.     2016-05-18 : JLF. Returns the image (like readfits). Added Status                 flag keyword.     2016-05-18 : JLF. Use red_anahdr2fits to create FITS headers from                 ANA headers.     2016-05-23 : JLF. Use red_filterchromisheaders to clean pt-grey                 headers. Use rdx_filetype.     2016-05-26 : THI. Allow reading of ana headers which are actually                 fits-headers.     2016-05-31 : JLF. Added silent keyword to suppress informational messages.     2016-06-08 : JLF. Bugfix, don't process headers if the user isn't asking 		 for them.     2016-05-30 : MGL. New keyword framenumber.     2016-08-12 : MGL. Read also momfbd-format files, return the                 mosaicked image.     2016-08-15 : MGL. Don't make header to be returned in header                 keyword, get it from red_readhead instead. Read only                 the parts of .momfbd files that are needed to make                 the mosaic.     2016-08-19 : MGL. Only test for .momfbd extension if filetype is                 not specified.     2016-08-31 : MGL. Use red_detectorname instead of red_getcamtag.                 Swap endian if needed. Remove byteorder keywords.     2016-11-04 : JLF. Added extension and tabkey keywords to support 		 reading from tab-HDUs and other extensions.     2016-12-07 : MGL. Use readfits so we can read 4-dimensional cubes.     2017-11-10 : MGL. Use the new /crop option with red_mozaic to get                 predictable dimensions.     2018-06-04 : MGL. Renamed keyword framenumber to nslice. Support                 compressed fits files.     2020-01-31 : MGL. New keywords rawstatistics and dark.     2020-03-31 : MGL. New keyword direction.     2025-01-30 : MGL. New keywords patch_indx and patch_coord.       The image contained in the file fname.   ");
  
  

libdata[libdataItem++] = new Array("./red_readdata_multiframe.html", "red_readdata_multiframe.pro", '.pro file in <a href="./dir-overview.html">./ directory</a>', "red_readdata_multiframe.pro", "", "", "", "", "          -1", "");
  
  
  libdata[libdataItem++] = new Array("./red_readdata_multiframe.html#red_readdata_multiframe", "red_readdata_multiframe", 'routine in <a href="./red_readdata_multiframe.html">red_readdata_multiframe.pro</a>', "red_readdata_multiframe.pro", "    Mats Löfdahl, Institute for Solar Physics   ", "red_readdata_multiframe", " Read data frames from multiple files. Assume all frames have the  same dimensions.   Keywords will be used when calling red_readdata for the individual  files.   ", "count      The number of frames in the returned cube.   date_beg      DATE-BEG keywords for all frames.   framenums      If given as input, frames with these frame numbers are       returned. As output, the frame numbers of the returned frames       or -1 for frames that were not read.   status      Status numbers for each file in fnames, 0 for success, -1 for       failure. .   _ref_extrafiles ", "SST pipeline", "   2022-08-22 : MGL. First version.     2022-12-22 : MGL. Allow the files to have multiple frames.     2024-09-06 : MGL. New keyword framenums.     2026-01-08 : MGL. New keyword count.       A datacube with the data from the files.   ");
  
  

libdata[libdataItem++] = new Array("./red_readhead.html", "red_readhead.pro", '.pro file in <a href="./dir-overview.html">./ directory</a>', "red_readhead.pro", "", "", "", "", "          -1", "");
  
  
  libdata[libdataItem++] = new Array("./red_readhead.html#red_readhead", "red_readhead", 'routine in <a href="./red_readhead.html">red_readhead.pro</a>', "red_readhead.pro", "     J. Lewis Fox, ISP, 2016-05-18   ", "red_readhead", " Read headers from data files in a camera independent way.   ", "filetype	The type of file to read. Allowed values are: 		fits 		fz                momfbd 	If not set auto-detection will be attempted.   date_beg       The timestamps for exposure start.   framenumbers       The framenumbers extracted from the file metadata.   select_frame       Specify to get header corresponding to a single frame in a        multi-frame image file.   noexternal       Set this to not read any external FITS header.   structheader	If set output the header as a structure.   status	Output the return status, 0 for success, -1 for failure.   silentextension	The name of the extension (EXTNAME) that we are interested in.   fname       The data file.   ", "CRISP pipeline", "   2016-05-18 : JLF. Created.     2016-05-31 : JLF. Added keyword silent to suppress informational                 messages.     2016-08-12 : MGL. Make header for momfbd-format file. New keyword                 framenumber. Call red_filterchromisheaders only for                 FITS files without SOLARNET header keyword. Call new                 function red_meta2head.     2016-08-19 : MGL. Only test for .momfbd extension if filetype is                 not specified.     2016-08-23 : MGL. Deal with ANA headers lacking data size                 information.     2016-08-31 : MGL. Use red_detectorname instead of red_getcamtag.                 Add rudimentary handling of tabulated DATE-BEG.     2016-09-01 : MGL. Change FRAME1 to FRAMENUM if needed.     2016-09-08 : MGL. Allow for headers without prefilter info (like                 darks).     2016-09-15 : MGL. Fix bug in construction of DATE-END from table.                 Fix bug in removal of empty lines. Also construct                 DATE-AVE. Construct DATE-BEG, DATE-END, and DATE-AVE                 only if they do not already exist. ANA files: get                 dimensions and data type from the first 256 bytes of                 the file.     2016-09-21 : MGL. Change filter tags to four-digit tags                 representing approximate filter wavelength.     2016-10-13 : MGL. Removed unnecessary check for W and H in ANA                 headers.     2016-10-19 : MGL. Look for data under /storage/ rather than under                 /mnt/ in Stockholm.     2016-11-05 : JLF. Read in extension headers using the extension                 keyword.     2017-03-10 : MGL. Move file-format specific code to their own                 subprograms. Trust rdx_filetype() to recognize momfbd                 files.     2017-03-16 : MGL. Look for (and optionally read) an external FITS                 header.     2017-09-01 : THI. Get date_beg and framenumbers from file. Rename                 keyword framenumber to select_frame.     2017-12-01 : MGL. Use status from red_readhead_fits.     2019-04-23 : MGL. Treat different file types more independently.        A FITS compatible header (from a data file of any instrument)   ");
  
  

libdata[libdataItem++] = new Array("./red_readhead_ana.html", "red_readhead_ana.pro", '.pro file in <a href="./dir-overview.html">./ directory</a>', "red_readhead_ana.pro", "", "", "", "", "          -1", "");
  
  
  libdata[libdataItem++] = new Array("./red_readhead_ana.html#red_readhead_ana", "red_readhead_ana", 'routine in <a href="./red_readhead_ana.html">red_readhead_ana.pro</a>', "red_readhead_ana.pro", "    Mats Löfdahl, ISP   ", "red_readhead_ana", " Return a fits-type header from an ANA fz format file.   ", "date_beg       The timestamps for exposure start.   framenumbers       The framenumbers extracted from the file metadata.   fname       The name of the data file.   ", "SST pipeline", "    2017-03-10 : MGL. Moved reading of headers from ANA fz format                  files from red_readhead.pro.      2018-06-04 : MGL. New keywords date_beg and framenumbers.      2019-04-05 : MGL. Import code from red_anahdr2fits.    ");
  
  

libdata[libdataItem++] = new Array("./red_readhead_db.html", "red_readhead_db.pro", '.pro file in <a href="./dir-overview.html">./ directory</a>', "red_readhead_db.pro", "    Oleksii Andriienko, Institute for Solar Physics   ", "", " This function constructs fits headers with help of information taken  from the database. It might substitute red_readhead function.   ", "", "SST pipeline", " 2019-05-28 : OA. First version.   2019-06-06 : OA. Rewritten. Loop for cameras added.   ");
  
  
  libdata[libdataItem++] = new Array("./red_readhead_db.html#red_readhead_db", "red_readhead_db", 'routine in <a href="./red_readhead_db.html">red_readhead_db.pro</a>', "red_readhead_db.pro", "", "red_readhead_db", "", "date_begframenumbersstatusfiles", "          -1", "");
  
  

libdata[libdataItem++] = new Array("./red_readhead_fits.html", "red_readhead_fits.pro", '.pro file in <a href="./dir-overview.html">./ directory</a>', "red_readhead_fits.pro", "", "", "", "", "          -1", "");
  
  
  libdata[libdataItem++] = new Array("./red_readhead_fits.html#red_readhead_fits", "red_readhead_fits", 'routine in <a href="./red_readhead_fits.html">red_readhead_fits.pro</a>', "red_readhead_fits.pro", "    Mats Löfdahl, ISP   ", "red_readhead_fits", " Return the header from a FITS format file, taking some  pipeline-specific issues into account.   ", "date_beg       The timestamps for exposure start.   extensionframenumbers       The framenumbers extracted from the file metadata.   select_frame       Only get meta-data for a specific frame. (TODO: implement)   silentstatus       0 is succeeded, -1 otherwise.   fname       The name of the data file.   ", "SST pipeline", "    2017-03-10 : MGL. Moved reading of headers from ANA fz format                  files from red_readhead.pro.      2017-03-13 : MGL. Deal with camera software OBS_PHDU bug.      2017-07-06 : THI. Use rdx_readhead to get header.      2017-09-01 : THI. Get date_beg and framenumbers from file.      2017-12-01 : MGL. New keyword status, use status from rdx_readhead.    ");
  
  

