  libdata[libdataItem++] = new Array("./red_rot_magn_align.html#red_rot_magn_align_deviation", "red_rot_magn_align_deviation", 'routine in <a href="./red_rot_magn_align.html">red_rot_magn_align.pro</a>', "red_rot_magn_align.pro", "    Mats Löfdahl, Institute for Solar Physics   ", "red_rot_magn_align_deviation", " Calculate model vs data deviation.   Helper function to red_rot_magn_align.   ", "im_ref      The reference image.   im_other      The image to be aligned to the reference image.   p     The parameter array.   ", "SST pipeline", "   2020-04-14 : MGL. First version.      The deviations.   ");
  
  libdata[libdataItem++] = new Array("./red_rot_magn_align.html#red_rot_magn_align", "red_rot_magn_align", 'routine in <a href="./red_rot_magn_align.html">red_rot_magn_align.pro</a>', "red_rot_magn_align.pro", "    Mats Löfdahl, Institute for Solar Physics   ", "red_rot_magn_align", " Find rotation, magnification, and alignment parameters that align  one image to another.   The images have to be fairly close to alignment on input. Just a few  degrees of rotation, a few percent of relative magnification, and a  shift of a few pixels. The images also have to have structures that  are similar in the two images and contain enough information to  determine a good match.   ", "display     Display some image data.   maxiterim_ref_in      The reference image.   im_in      Image to be aligned to the reference image.   ", "SST pipeline", "   2020-04-14 : MGL. First version.      Parameters that make the image match the reference image as well    as possible: [angle (deg), relative magnification, x shift, y    shift]   ");
  
  

libdata[libdataItem++] = new Array("./red_rotate.html", "red_rotate.pro", '.pro file in <a href="./dir-overview.html">./ directory</a>', "red_rotate.pro", "", "", "", "", "          -1", "");
  
  
  libdata[libdataItem++] = new Array("./red_rotate.html#red_rotate", "red_rotate", 'routine in <a href="./red_rotate.html">red_rotate.pro</a>', "red_rotate.pro", "    Mats Löfdahl, Institute for Solar Physics   ", "red_rotate", " Wrapper for IDL's rotate() function, adding an inverse flag.  Also handling image cubes.   ", "inverse       Do the inverse operation. Note: if direction is negative and        the inverse keyword is set, this is equivalent to calling with        abs(direction) and not setting inverse.   dir       The value of direction that would give the same operation        without /inverse.   array       The image to be rotated. For arrays with more than two        dimensions, the first two dimensions will be rotated.   direction       Defines the operation to be performed, see documentation for        rotate(). If negative, the inverse operation is performed.   ", "SST pipeline", "   2019-12-09 : MGL. First version.     2020-03-16 : MGL. Accept negative direction.     2020-04-01 : MGL. Handle image cubes.       Returns the rotated and/or transposed image(s).   ");
  
  

libdata[libdataItem++] = new Array("./red_rotation.html", "red_rotation.pro", '.pro file in <a href="./dir-overview.html">./ directory</a>', "red_rotation.pro", "", "", "", "", "          -1", "");
  
  
  libdata[libdataItem++] = new Array("./red_rotation.html#red_rotation", "red_rotation", 'routine in <a href="./red_rotation.html">red_rotation.pro</a>', "red_rotation.pro", "    J. de la Cruz Rodriguez & M. Löfdahl, Institute for Solar Physics   ", "red_rotation", " ", "background      The full-FOV array is padded with this value.   full      Use this keyword to make full FOV cubes without clipping of       corners, otherwise the rotated and shifted frame will be of the       original size. Should be array with the following elements:       [maxangle, mdx0, mdx1, mdy0, mdy1 [, angles]], where elements       [1:4] are the max shifts in all directions.   stretch_grid       stretch grid computed with red_gridmatch (2, nTiles_x, nTiles_y)   nthreads       Number of threads to use during the interpolation   neareststretch_matrixunrotated_shifts        Array of 2 elements or distorsion grid measured before         derrotating the images.   img       The image to be shifted and rotated.   angle      Rotation angle in radians.   sdx      Shift in the X direction.   sdy      Shift in the Y direction.   ", "CRISP pipeline", "   2013-06-04 : Split from monolithic version of crispred.pro.     2013-06-10 : MGL. Made using bicubic interpolation with -0.5 the                 default and introduced a new flag for linear                 interpolation.     2014-05-05 : JdlCR. Error in the definition of dx, dy found. The                 shifts should be applied inside the parenthesis.     2014-11-29 : JdlCR. Added support for fullframe cubes (aka,                 despite rotation and shifts, the entire FOV is inside                 the image)     2019-03-19 : MGL. New keyword background.     2020-06-22 : MGL. Use entire range of angles to calculate                 dimensions of rotated image iff keyword full is given                 with more than 5 elements. Also fix bug so shifts are                 added before rotation for the same calculation.     2020-10-01 : JdlCR. Modified this routine to a) only allow                 bilinear o nearest neighbor interpolation and                 b) to allow including the stretch correction                 in this interpolation so all corrections are                 applied at once. Use our own interpolation routines.     2021-02-07 : JdlCR. Introduced unrotated_shifts, in order to                 apply shifts that were measured before derotation.       The shifted and rotated image.   ");
  
  

